cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "search-as-code: an agentic retrieval harness with one primitive API over any vector database"
abstract: >-
  Search-as-Code is a code-mode retrieval harness: instead of calling a fixed search endpoint,
  the LLM writes a short Python program against a unified primitive API, executed in a sandbox
  with intermediate state kept out of the model context. The same program runs over any vector
  database. The repository also contains the controlled experiments behind the claims, and an
  audit log of their limitations.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "search-as-code contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/oro-jackson/searchascode-sdk"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - agentic retrieval
  - code mode
  - vector search
  - information retrieval
